[00:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to the anti-gravity A1 first flight tutorial video. Preparing for your first flight. Remove the drone from the carry case. [music] When using the battery for the'

[00:19] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A charging hub for Antigravity A1 batteries is shown, with green indicator lights.
AUDIO: 'first time, you need to charge and activate it first. You can charge the battery by inserting it into the drone and connecting a USBC cable or by placing it in the charging hub. [music] When the battery indicator light is on,'

[00:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it means the battery has been activated. Use the same method to activate the batteries for the grip controller and vision goggles. [music] Before your first flight, we recommend charging all devices to full power. Tap the power'

[00:47] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: Close-up of the Antigravity A1 Vision Goggles, showing a diopter adjustment knob and a connected cable.
AUDIO: 'button on each device to check its charge level. Make sure the battery is fully charged. Use the vision goggles USBC to DC power cable to connect the goggles battery and'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'attach the battery lanyard to the carabiner. Choose an open unobstructed outdoor area before takeoff. Press then long press the power button'

[01:13] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: The Antigravity A1 drone is placed on a branded landing pad.
AUDIO: 'for 2 seconds to turn on the drone. [music] The drone will automatically extend its landing gear. If the landing gear does not extend automatically, you can manually extend it and then place'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the drone on the ground, protecting the underside lens. You can also extend the landing gear manually and place the drone on the ground before turning it on.'

[01:37] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A hand holds and operates the Antigravity A1 Grip Controller, highlighting its buttons and trigger.
AUDIO: '[music] Place the drone away from you. Press, then press, and hold the vision goggles battery button for two seconds to turn them on. Press, then press and hold the grip'

[01:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'controller for two seconds to turn it on. Unfold the vision goggles antennas. Put on the vision goggles. Adjust the fit of the head strap using'

[02:02] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A person wears the Antigravity A1 Vision Goggles, adjusting them.
AUDIO: 'the Velcro on the goggles. If your vision ranges from plus 2.00 diopters, far-sighted to minus 5.00 diopters nearsighted, you can fine-tune the focus by rotating the diopter'

[02:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adjustment knobs. Close one eye first and rotate the corresponding knob until the [music] image appears clear. Then open that [music] eye and close the other one, adjusting again until the'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'image is clear. Finally, move the knob sideways to adjust the interpupilary distance until the images from both lenses merge into one.'

[02:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Normally, the three devices are already paired at the factory. If your vision goggles do not display a video feed after powering on, please follow these'

[02:55] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: The Antigravity A1 Vision Goggles are shown on a table, with antennas unfolded and a cable connected.
AUDIO: 'steps to synchronize your devices. We do this by powering on each device and enter standby mode. [music] Press and hold the power button on the drone. the home button on the left side of the'

[03:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'vision goggles and the power button on the grip controller at the same time to enter pairing mode. [music]'

[03:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The three devices will emit sounds while pairing. Once the sounds stop, pairing is complete and the goggles will display the drone\'s live view. [music] Next, check the'

[03:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'flight interface in the goggles. After confirming there are no error messages and that the GNSS signal is strong, the upper part of the interface will display'

[03:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ready to take off. You can now begin your flight. Please fly in a flat, open, obstacle-free area where possible. When flying, be mindful of your footing and give yourself ample space.'

[04:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Push the slider upward twice to start the drone\'s motors. Then continue pushing the slider upward. The drone'

[04:12] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: The Antigravity A1 drone is shown flying, with green lights visible on its body.
AUDIO: 'will automatically take off, ascend to about 1.2 m, and hover in place. [music] To land, push the slider downward continuously. The drone will automatically descend,'

[04:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'land safely, and stop its motors. You can control the drone using the'

[04:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'accelerator and slider on the grip controller. The slider controls the drone\'s ascent and descent at a fixed speed. [music] The navigation dot displayed in the'

[04:53] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A split screen shows an aerial view of the drone flying over water on the left, and the vision goggles' FPV display on the right, showing flight data.
AUDIO: 'vision goggles follows your hand movements. Pulling the accelerator makes the drone fly toward the navigation dot. The harder you pull, the faster it flies. [music]'

[05:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The drone\'s nose will always face the same direction as the navigation dot. You can move your arm to change the direction of the navigation dot. [music] While hovering, use the 360 view dial to'

[05:18] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The vision goggles' FPV display is shown with an overlay indicating "Front view of the drone" and various flight metrics.
AUDIO: 'adjust the drone\'s orientation. During flight, you can freely look around in 360° without affecting the drone\'s flight'

[05:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'direction. [music] If your view doesn\'t match the flight direction, a small window at the top of the goggles will display the drone\'s front view for reference. [music] To quickly sync the flight direction'

[05:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with your current view, press the 360 view dial. The drone will instantly align its nose with your viewing direction. [music] When you release the accelerator trigger, the drone will stop and hover'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in place. You can also press the brake RTH button at any time to bring the drone to an immediate stop. The drone has three flight modes:'

[06:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'normal, sport, [music] and cinematic. By default, the drone operates in normal mode. Flight speeds vary between modes.'

[06:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Each mode is controlled the same way. By default, the drone starts in video mode after being powered on. Open menu, shooting parameters to switch shooting modes. Select video resolution'

[06:41] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A split screen shows the grip controller being operated on the left, and the vision goggles' FPV display on the right, showing the drone's perspective.
AUDIO: 'and frame rate or adjust camera parameters such as shutter speed and white balance. Press the record button to start recording.'

[06:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Press the photo button during recording. To capture a photo using the current video resolution, press the record button again to stop recording.'

[07:06] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A split screen shows the grip controller being operated on the left, and the vision goggles' FPV display on the right, showing the drone's perspective over a coastal area.
AUDIO: 'Press and hold the photo button for 2 seconds to switch to photo mode. Press the photo button to capture a photo. Press and hold the record button for two'

[07:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'seconds while in photo mode to switch back to video mode. [music] When taking off or during flight once the GNSS signal icon turns white,'

[07:31] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: The vision goggles' FPV display shows a wide view of the ocean with wind turbines, displaying flight data like speed, altitude, and battery.
AUDIO: 'the drone automatically saves its current location as the home point. After successful recording, [music] the flight interface will display a message indicating that the return point has'

[07:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'been updated. During flight, the home H icon remains visible, representing the most recently saved home point. To activate return to home, press and hold the brake your RTH'

[07:58] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: A split screen shows the grip controller being operated on the left, and the vision goggles' FPV display on the right, showing the drone's perspective over a rocky beach.
AUDIO: 'button on the grip controller [music] to trigger return to home. The drone will automatically return to the last recorded home [music] point. While returning, press the brake RTH button.'

[08:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To cancel, return to home and regain manual control of the drone. Thanks for watching.'
